-- prompt.md --
Implement `to_roman(number)` and `from_roman(text)` in `numerals/roman.py`.

- They cover 1 to 3999 and use the standard subtractive forms (IV, IX, XL, XC, CD, CM).
- `to_roman` raises `ValueError` for any number outside 1 to 3999.
- `from_roman` accepts only canonical upper-case numerals: anything else (the empty string, "IIII", "VX", "IC", "MMMM", letters that are not numerals) raises `ValueError`.
- `from_roman(to_roman(n)) == n` for every n in range.
